From: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: wait for TX to drain in airoha_dev_stop

Rebased onto upstream's new airoha_gdm_dev refactor (920-xx merged
2026-05-27, commit d22ceb8d24). Upstream already does ref-counted DMA
shutdown via atomic_dec_and_test, but does not wait for in-flight TX
to complete before clearing GLOBAL_CFG_TX_DMA_EN_MASK. Add a bounded
poll on GLOBAL_CFG_TX_DMA_BUSY_MASK so the DMA isn't yanked from under
hardware that still has packets in flight.

Differences from the pre-rebase 628:
- Drops the NAPI lifecycle reshuffle (upstream keeps NAPI on permanently
  at probe time, so the per-interface start/stop dance is no longer
  required).
- Drops the netdev_tx_reset_subqueue reorder (upstream already does this
  earlier in the stop path).
- On timeout, warn and continue (not -ETIMEDOUT return) so phylink_stop
  still runs and the interface gets fully torn down regardless.

Signed-off-by: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2045,6 +2045,18 @@
 					    FE_PSE_PORT_DROP);
 
 	if (atomic_dec_and_test(&qdma->users)) {
+		u32 val;
+		int err;
+
+		/* Wait for TX to drain before clearing the DMA enable bits. */
+		err = read_poll_timeout(airoha_qdma_rr, val,
+					!(val & GLOBAL_CFG_TX_DMA_BUSY_MASK),
+					USEC_PER_MSEC, 100 * USEC_PER_MSEC,
+					false, qdma, REG_QDMA_GLOBAL_CFG);
+		if (err)
+			netdev_warn(netdev,
+				    "TX did not drain in 100ms before DMA shutdown\n");
+
 		airoha_qdma_clear(qdma, REG_QDMA_GLOBAL_CFG,
 				  GLOBAL_CFG_TX_DMA_EN_MASK |
 				  GLOBAL_CFG_RX_DMA_EN_MASK);
